  The same terms are stated in the data itself. The _meta block at the head of each of Features.json, Instructions.json and
  Registers.json reads:

    "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved."
    "info": "This document is Non-confidential and licensed under the BSD 3-clause license."

  The README.md of the package reads:

    This package contains a subset of the information provided in the packages with Arm proprietary licenses. Content that is not
    currently in a machine-readable format, as well as all descriptive content, is omitted.

    The [notice](docs/notice.html) gives details of the license terms and conditions under which this package is provided.

  Arm's proprietary packages of the same data carry other terms. Arm's blog post "Getting started with AARCHMRS Features.json using
  Python" (developer.arm.com, architectures and processors blog) says of them: "Re-use is only permitted for informational and
  non-commercial or personal use only." Only the BSD package is used here.

what the conditions mean for masc
  1 and 2: the licence text and the copyright line travel with the vendored copy in gen/vendor/aarchmrs/LICENSE and in masc's NOTICE,
  which is shipped with masc in source and binary form.
  3: neither Arm's name nor its contributors' names are used to endorse masc.

what is vendored
  upstream  https://developer.arm.com/-/cdn-downloads/permalink/Exploration-Tools-OS-Machine-Readable-Data/AARCHMRS_BSD/AARCHMRS_OPENSOURCE_A_profile_FAT-2026-09.tar.gz
  release   2026-09_rel, schema 2.9.6, build 868, architecture "vFATAp2-A", built 2026-09-21 13:58:23 (from the _meta of the data)
  package   sha256 d5bf3f538663fb18be081ba8e9f08b188ed06f81dd19d4aa2da5b2795103a4ec
  copied    the release tarball itself, unmodified, as gen/vendor/aarchmrs/AARCHMRS_OPENSOURCE_A_profile_FAT-2026-09.tar.gz, with LICENSE
            written from docs/notice.html. The tarball holds Features.json, Instructions.json, Registers.json, README.md, schema/ and docs/.
  why       Instructions.json is 111 MB and Registers.json 92 MB unpacked, and GitHub refuses a file over 100 MB. The tarball is 5.7 MB and
            its sha-256 is Arm's own, so the copy can be compared with the download by hand. A reader of the data unpacks it in memory.

limits of the source
  The BSD package of this release is a FAT build: its architecture field reads "vFATAp2-A", the A-profile architecture plus Arm's
  future architecture technologies (FAT). A table generator selects the extensions masc supports and does not take the whole file.
  Descriptions are redacted in the BSD package, so the data holds encodings, assembly rules, operations and registers but not the
  text of the Architecture Reference Manual.
  Instructions.json carries A64, A32 and T32. masc reads A64 only.

how it is checked
  The source is a row of gen's source table with this revision and the checksum of the vendored tree, so gen --check refuses a copy
  that has changed. Nothing is fetched at generation time. A later release is a new copy and a new row in one commit.
